# Rule 02. Primitives, HTML5 and ARIA

Source: `codegen-x/ui8kit:.cursor/rules/02-no-raw-html.mdc`, `03-static-aria.mdc`, runtime appendices
`runtime-{svelte,react,vue}.mdc`, `packages/ui-gates`.

## Scope: every layer

These rules apply to prototypes, layouts and apps alike, including app screens and taste screens (rule 00, three
layers). Brand freedom of app screens covers spacing and look, never the tags: a screen is built from the framework's
UI8Kit primitives with the `tag` retag, by the UI8Kit contracts.

- Framework special elements that render no host tag are not bare tags: `<svelte:window>`, `<svelte:document>`,
  `<svelte:body>`, `<svelte:head>`, `<svelte:options>` (the rules gate skips them). `<svelte:element this>` is a dynamic
  tag and is not allowed.
- Inline `svg`, `path`, `img`, `canvas` in composition are bare tags too: icons go through the kit's icon primitive
  (Lucide), images through the image primitive. Raw markup is allowed only inside the kit zone (primitives, icon
  glyph registry, utils), which is never scanned.

## Primitives only

1. Composition contains zero raw native tags (lowercase HTML/SVG elements). Use the kit: `Box`, `Stack`, `Group`,
   `Grid` instead of `div`; `Text`, `Inline`, `Title` instead of `p`/`span`/`h1`..`h6`; `List`/`ListItem`; `Form`,
   `Label`, inputs; `Button` with `variant`/`size`; `Card`; landmarks via `Block tag`.
2. No raw HTML injection (`{@html}`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `v-html`) and no dynamic tag
   (`<svelte:element this>`, `<component :is>`, `createElement(tag)`).
3. Missing tag: search the kit primitives, then the kit's tag groups; else add a primitive to the kit (its spec for
   a generated kit). Never fall back to a raw tag. Never edit generated or installed kit files by hand.
4. `Box`/`Text` `tag` only from the HTML5 allowlist (`ui-gates source`, rule `tag-allowlist`).

## HTML5 and ARIA

1. Native HTML5 semantics first; ARIA only where the element cannot express the role.
2. In composition an `aria-*` state is static. State reaches ARIA only through a primitive prop
   (`<Button pressed={on}>`). Naming attributes (`aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`, ...) may be
   expressions from content or props.
3. ARIA goes through `Attrs`/attributes; there are no role props. Screens never write `data-ui8kit*` by hand.
4. Dialogs have a name, a description, Escape close and focus return. Keep the kit focus ring.

Enforced: rules gate detectors `raw-native-tag`, `raw-html`, `dynamic-tag`, `reactive-aria`;
`ui-gates source <dirs>` (raw tag where a primitive exists, tag allowlist); `ui-gates html <cases.json>`
(html-validate + axe-core in jsdom; config `rules/html-validate.json`, preset `html-validate:recommended`).
